# base.inp -- lower-atmosphere handoff for the mol_diffusion regression case.
# Copied unchanged (values pinned) from mol_base_handoff/base.inp; only this
# header differs, because here He_diffusion is on and Kzz_base is live.
#
# Planet: the Tier-2 gate hot Uranus (docs/lower_atmosphere_figs/data_g2),
# 0.0457 M_J, R_p = 0.49 R_J, T_eq = 1140 K, He/H = 0.0793,
# "Molecular chemistry: True" (which couples the molecular base on).
#
# T_base / r_base / HeH_base repeat the values input.inp already carries, so
# the handoff does not move the planet: the case isolates the base COMPOSITION
# path, not a change of base state.  Kzz_base is the 1e9 cm^2/s that
# src/utils/vulcan_to_base.py writes; here it is live, and it repeats the
# "He_Kzz: 1.0e9" of input.inp so the two sources cannot disagree.
#
# q_H2_base is the point of this case: > 0 selects the photochemical branch of
# h2_mixing_ratio_base(), so comp_ntot_bc() removes the H nuclei bound into H2
# using this value instead of the Visscher/Koskinen chemical-equilibrium fit.
# 0.84 is the value Koskinen et al. (2022, ApJ 929, 52, section 3.2) report at
# the lower boundary of the model this gate reproduces: "The volume mixing
# ratio of H2 at the lower boundary is about q0 = 0.84 while H is a minor
# species with q0 = 0.026."  It sits below the equilibrium fit at the same
# (p, T), so the two branches give different ntot_bc and the regression detects
# it if the precedence is ever lost, and below the ceiling 0.5/(0.5 + He/H) =
# 0.863 that this He/H can supply.
#
# p_base is the base LEVEL, and since 2026-09-03 it is what fixes it: input.inp
# no longer carries "Log10 lower boundary number density", and startup derives
# n0 = p_base/(k_B T0 ntot_bc) instead (input_read.f90, "the base level has one
# source").  1e-6 bar is the level of the handoff this gate reproduces --
# Koskinen et al. (2022) section 3.2: "The lower boundary of the model is at
# r0 = 1.34Rp (p0 = 10-6 bar, T0 = 1,140 K)" -- and it is the level the gate's
# own base radius already corresponded to.  Before that date the file said
# 1e-5 bar while the density key put the base at 9e-6 bar, and nothing checked
# the two against each other (docs/p44_base_sawtooth.md sections 9.1 and 9.3).
T_base    1140.0
r_base    0.49
HeH_base  0.0793
Kzz_base  1.000e+09
q_H2_base 0.84
p_base    1.000e-06
